---
import './figures.css';
---
<figure class="cl-figure" data-survival aria-labelledby="survival-title">
  <figcaption id="survival-title"><span class="cl-number">Figure 5</span> Remove a region from the product range</figcaption>
  <div class="cl-panel">
    <div class="cl-controls"><label>Survival goal <select data-goal aria-label="Survival goal"><option value="zone">Zone failure</option><option value="region">Region failure</option></select></label><label>Unavailable <select data-failure aria-label="Unavailable domain"><option value="none">None</option><option value="West-1">West zone 1</option><option value="West">West region</option><option value="North">North region</option><option value="East">East region</option></select></label></div>
    <p class="cl-label">One illustrative range · products home West</p>
    <div class="cl-three" data-regions data-live></div>
    <div class="cl-banner" data-count data-live></div>
    <p class="cl-explanation" data-result data-live aria-live="polite"></p>
  </div>
  <p class="cl-caption">Structural models of the standard three-region regional-table policies, after placement has converged. Every voter occupies a separate node and zone. The region-survival arrangement gives West two voters, North two and East one; the remote two and one can be exchanged. The count assumes survivors communicate and their storage works. It does not time detection, election, lease transfer or requests.</p>
  <details><summary>Layouts and counts as text</summary><p>Zone survival: three West voters, majority two; one non-voter in North and one in East. West zone 1 lost leaves two voters. West region lost leaves zero voters, even though two non-voting copies remain. Losing North or East leaves three voters.</p><p>Region survival: five voters, majority three, placed West two, North two and East one. Losing West or North leaves three voters; losing East leaves four. At least one remote vote is required to complement West’s two local voters in healthy operation.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
document.querySelectorAll('[data-survival]').forEach(root=>{
  const goal=root.querySelector('[data-goal]') as HTMLSelectElement;
  const fail=root.querySelector('[data-failure]') as HTMLSelectElement;
  const draw=()=>{
    const region=goal.value==='region', lost=fail.value;
    const layout=region?{North:2,West:2,East:1}:{North:0,West:3,East:0};
    let surviving=0;
    root.querySelector('[data-regions]').innerHTML=Object.entries(layout).map(([name,n])=>{
      const gone=lost===name;
      const voters=Array.from({length:n},(_,i)=>{
        const unavailable=gone||lost===`${name}-${i+1}`;
        if(!unavailable) surviving++;
        return `<span class="cl-voter${unavailable?' cl-unavailable':''}"><span${unavailable?' class="cl-crossed"':''}>Zone ${i+1} · voter</span>${unavailable?' · unavailable':''}</span>`;
      }).join('');
      return `<div class="cl-region${gone?' cl-lost':''}"><strong>${name}${name==='West'?' · home':''}${gone?' · unavailable':''}</strong>${voters||`<span class="cl-voter cl-nonvoter${gone?' cl-unavailable':''}"><span${gone?' class="cl-crossed"':''}>Non-voter</span>${gone?' · unavailable':''}</span>`}</div>`;
    }).join('');
    const total=region?5:3, majority=region?3:2, good=surviving>=majority;
    root.querySelector('[data-count]').textContent=`${surviving} surviving voters · majority ${majority} of ${total} configured voters`;
    root.querySelector('[data-result]').textContent=good?`${surviving} voters can reach the required ${majority}. The range has a quorum path, allowing any necessary leadership and lease changes. ${region?'A majority cannot be formed entirely within West.':'Non-voters add no votes.'}`:`The range cannot reach ${majority} votes. North and East’s non-voting copies do not replace the missing West voters. Data copies can survive while ordinary reads and writes become unavailable.`;
  };
  goal.addEventListener('change',draw); fail.addEventListener('change',draw); draw();
});
</script>
